it's another week of children going to  school in zimbabwe and doing nothing  constructive because there are no staff  the government suspended thousands of  teachers for three months without pay  for going on strike demanding more money  we are not learning we are now playing  there are no teachers we are now roaming  around  the government has offered teachers a 20  pay increase payment of part of their  salaries in u.s dollars and other  incentives including free education for  their children and loans for housing but  unions rejected the offer saying it's  still not enough the government here  employs about 140 000 teachers  nationwide it's not known exactly how  many of them are on strike the education  department says they can be replaced  with thousands of unemployed teachers  currently looking for work  union leaders believe politicians are  out of touch with reality  those who are supposed to manage our  education  have found an escape route where their  own children are leading in private  schools in elite private schools and  some of them are learning in exotic  learning centers beating australia u.s  among other listeners but so the public  school is now so much neglected because  they are not affected their sons and  daughters are not there so they don't  worry  munara dimasiwa sells gas from his house  to supplement his income  he and other suspended teachers want at  least 540 us dollars a month  right now they're earning less than 100  a teacher gets about 80 u.s a right now  and you need to break that amount into  transport allowance there is the housing  allowance  and the basic salary is also included in  that 80 us  economists warn paying salaries in  american dollars will fuel inflation  with no side so far willing to budge  there is little to no learning taking  place in many of zimbabwe's public  schools haru mutasa al jazeera
 

